From 4f18ea3875435100768925da15e0813800371f86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:36:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Show a job's progress as a notice that stays, in the theme's
 style

The progress panel reused the menu's download box: a narrow box in the top
corner that a theme with its own notices leaves without a background, over
the header, cutting its text. An outside job's progress is now one of the
theme's notices that stays: its title beside the icon, a detail line and a
gauge, at the full width of the style, until the job closes it.
POST /progress-notice replaces POST /progress.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
